        "narrative": "<p>The lake trout catch was above the normal range for lakes of this ecological class, and was higher than the catch in the 1980 survey.  Several year classes were represented in the catch, with the strongest being the 1987 and 1986 year classes.  Growth of age-6 lake trout was above average for lakes of this area, but the growth of age-3 fish had been somewhat below average.The white sucker catch was within the normal range for lakes of this class, and two burbot were collected.  Northern pike and yellow perch have been collected in this lake in the past, but none were taken in this assessment.</p>",
